0013: def main(input_grid):
0014:     """
0015:     Fill black regions enclosed by green boundaries with yellow while preserving the original boundary.
0016: 
0017:     Input structure:
0018:     - The input is a square black grid containing one or more green closed shapes.
0019:     - Green pixels form the visible boundaries of enclosed regions.
0020:     - Black pixels may appear both inside and outside those boundaries.
0021: 
0022:     Rule:
0023:     - Detect the interior of the green objects.
0024:     - Exclude the green boundary pixels themselves.
0025:     - Recolor enclosed black interior pixels yellow and leave all other pixels unchanged.
0026: 
0027:     Key insight:
0028:     - The transformation depends on topology rather than shape identity: only black cells
0029:       trapped inside a green boundary are changed.
